  "metadata": {
    "title": "Layer thicknesses, layer attitudes, CRISM, and DTMs of Becquerel Crater",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10727125",
    "publication_date": "2022",
    "description": "<p>*VERSION UPDATE FEB 29 2024: The long-wavelength \"L\" CRISM cube of FRT000243D0_07 was unfortunately left out in the first version of this dataset (only the \"S\" cube had been included). This update also includes the \"L\" cube. My sincere apologies for the confusion.<br><br>This is the dataset associated with the paper \"Protracted Hydrogeological Activity in Arabia Terra, Mars: Evidence from the Structure and Mineralogy of the Layered Deposits of Becquerel Crater\" in the Journal of Geophysical Research: Planets.<br><br>Schmidt, G.,&nbsp;Luzzi, E., Rossi, A.,&nbsp;Pondrelli, M.,&nbsp;Apuzzo, A.,&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Salvini, F. (2022).&nbsp;Protracted Hydrogeological Activity in Arabia Terra, Mars: Evidence from the Structure and Mineralogy of the Layered Deposits of Becquerel Crater. Journal of Geophysical Research: Planets.<br><br>This dataset includes layer thickness and layer attitude measurements of sedimentary structures within Becquerel crater, Mars. The accompanying digital terrain models used to acquire these measurements are also included. A free version of the Orion layer attitude measuring software is also included with instructions of use. The CRISM cubes and accompanying&nbsp;.roi files from ENVI (regions of interest used to produce the spectrum presented in the published paper) are included.&nbsp;</p>",
